= Appendix D — Rules and Calculations

== D.1 Practical calculations

*Pulse:* estimate beats per minute by multiplying a 15-second count by four. For example, 18 beats in 15 seconds gives an estimated 72 beats per minute. Measurement technique and irregular rhythms may affect the estimate.

*Training time:* multiply the number of sessions by their duration when all sessions are equal. Four 30-minute sessions total 120 minutes.

*Speed:* distance divided by time, using consistent units. A 100-metre run in 20 seconds has an average speed of 5 metres per second. Actual speed can vary during the run.

*Round-robin fixtures:* when each of n teams plays each other once, the number of matches is n(n − 1) / 2. Four teams make 6 matches. Extra legs or finals change the count.

== D.2 Rules and safety

Competition rules change and vary by governing body and level. Read the question's stated rules and use current official rules for actual events. Clear throwing sectors, suitable equipment, supervision, accessible routes and appropriate warm-up all support safer activity, but no precaution guarantees that injury cannot occur.
